# CVE Notes — selected high-impact vulnerabilities

## CVE-2021-44228 — Log4Shell
Category: Software and Data Integrity Failures (A08).
CVSSv3: 10.0.
Apache Log4j 2 versions 2.0-beta9 through 2.14.1 evaluate JNDI lookup strings
found in logged messages. An attacker who can cause a vulnerable application
to log an attacker-controlled string (User-Agent, X-Forwarded-For, form input)
can achieve unauthenticated remote code execution via LDAP or RMI callback.

## CVE-2017-0144 — EternalBlue (MS17-010)
Category: Vulnerable and Outdated Components (A06).
CVSSv3: 8.1.
SMBv1 in Microsoft Windows allows a remote attacker to execute code via
crafted packets that mishandle transaction structures. Basis for WannaCry
and NotPetya. Patched in MS17-010. Legacy Windows Server 2003/2008
without patch is trivially owned.

## CVE-2014-0160 — Heartbleed
Category: Cryptographic Failures (A02).
CVSSv3: 7.5.
OpenSSL 1.0.1 through 1.0.1f mis-parses the TLS heartbeat extension length,
allowing a remote attacker to read up to 64 KB of process memory per request.
Leaked private keys and session cookies. Mitigation: upgrade OpenSSL, rotate
keys, revoke certificates.

## CVE-2019-0708 — BlueKeep
Category: Vulnerable and Outdated Components (A06).
CVSSv3: 9.8.
Windows RDP pre-auth use-after-free in older Windows versions (7, Server 2008
R2, XP, Server 2003). Wormable. Enable NLA and patch or block TCP/3389.

## CVE-2021-34527 — PrintNightmare
Category: Security Misconfiguration (A05).
CVSSv3: 8.8.
Windows Print Spooler allows a remote authenticated attacker to load an
arbitrary DLL via crafted RPC calls, gaining SYSTEM. Mitigations: disable
the Print Spooler on servers that do not need it, restrict Point and Print.

## CVE-2020-1472 — Zerologon
Category: Identification and Authentication Failures (A07).
CVSSv3: 10.0.
Netlogon MS-NRPC uses AES-CFB8 with an all-zero IV, letting an unauthenticated
attacker on the network set the domain-controller machine account password to
empty, escalating to Domain Admin. Patch and monitor Netlogon events 4742.

## CVE-2022-30190 — Follina
Category: Injection (A03).
CVSSv3: 7.8.
Microsoft Support Diagnostic Tool (MSDT) URL handler executes attacker-supplied
PowerShell when a Word document references an ms-msdt: URI. Delivered via
phishing. Disable the ms-msdt handler in the registry as a workaround.

## CVE-2023-23397 — Outlook NTLM Leak
Category: Broken Access Control (A01).
CVSSv3: 9.8.
Microsoft Outlook processes a crafted meeting invite that references a UNC
path in PidLidReminderFileParameter, causing the client to send NTLMv2 to
attacker-controlled SMB. Relayable to internal services. Zero-click.
